the aftermath of yet another russian  missile strike in kharkiv  this mainly russian-speaking city  ukraine's second largest has suffered  some of the worst shelling since  russia's invasion more than seven weeks  ago  emergency services say at least one  person was killed and many more injured  in this attack that caused the fire to  spread into residential areas  around 11 o'clock today the emergency  services received a message that an  enemy missile had hit a five-story  administrative building a rescue team in  tanker trucks was dispatched to the  scene  in the town of trotsyarnet in the sunmi  region northwest of kharkiv  families gathered to mourn some of the  latest victims  the un says that more than 1900  civilians have been killed including at  least 162 children since the war started  russian forces laid mines in the  cemetery before withdrawing from the  area a couple of weeks ago  a father cries over his dead son's grave  civilians and soldiers are buried here  we held a funeral for my son when they  liberated trotsky next  we were afraid thinking maybe some of  the russian fascists are still here and  they'll blow up the grave  we put a photo of him there how he  always was always smiling always  cheerful always positive  hundreds of kilometers away in the  western city of levive where local  authorities say four russian missiles  were intercepted on saturday morning  volunteers prepared humanitarian aid  please do not  stop helping us do not stop providing us  with humanitarian assistance because  more and more people are  fleeing  their homes and they need your help  please don't stop helping us  after a second attack in two days on a  ukrainian weapons facility in the  capital kiev the ukrainian military  warned of potentially more to come  due to the presence of russian warships  armed with sea launched cruise missiles  in the black sea there is an increased  threat of the occupiers using missile  arms against the defense industrial  facilities and logistics infrastructure  of our state  bodies lie on the streets in the  besieged port city of mariopol where  russian forces again said they had taken  full control of a steel plant  the ukrainian army denies that saying  marines and members of the azov  battalion are still defending their  positions  in the giant soviet-built factory  in a city almost completely destroyed  and from where thousands of civilians  have been unable to escape  the ukrainian president vladimir  zelinsky is warning russia not to in his  words eliminate the last remaining  ukrainian soldiers inside the besieged  city of mariopol or it will be the end  of peace talks  peace talks that the russian president  vladimir putin recently described as  having reached a dead end  chance trafford al jazeera kiev
 

